{"edition_id":"urn:uuid:35b4350d-7202-5d47-8b85-5262d7ca441c","id":"urn:uuid:30220403-5a3c-58b2-9edc-b35749d89fa9","order":1,"protected_tokens":[],"record_type":"segment","rights_id":"urn:uuid:52a7c815-5b13-5f21-a52a-e7fa11238e07","schema_id":"ttna-segment-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","semantic_slot":"title","source_block_sha256":"145ef61b4910285904a3e8d16eeca60dcc0c077d8d4bc09ae4bb3b01823793c7","source_file_id":"urn:uuid:271e812b-1ccd-53ed-a402-07fe58709c8a","source_locale":"en-US","source_locator":{"end_line":655,"layout":"Section*","layout_ordinal":35,"start_line":653},"source_text":"Acknowledgments","source_text_sha256":"4be0f860ee3560910d50596233fe802eeecf0972c7a9de427a76ae9a622e2ea1","translation_state":"source_frozen","unit_id":"urn:uuid:ba0206aa-b20f-54ce-b69e-4fdf460ce7dc"}
{"edition_id":"urn:uuid:35b4350d-7202-5d47-8b85-5262d7ca441c","id":"urn:uuid:35ffe0ed-c9a1-51ae-97eb-2b4275513960","order":4,"protected_tokens":[{"header":"Quotes eld","kind":"Quotes","ordinal":1,"sha256":"0c543e8f69a254076b2000cb6d4163dc1bfee14405a93b4a2c525aafb3ce2301"},{"header":"Quotes erd","kind":"Quotes","ordinal":2,"sha256":"f2256e820d421d857519a647df2247b25fd7f42c4ff3e95cb335b9287e332f84"}],"record_type":"segment","rights_id":"urn:uuid:52a7c815-5b13-5f21-a52a-e7fa11238e07","schema_id":"ttna-segment-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","semantic_slot":"paragraph","source_block_sha256":"90f9e0959e524541e220cf3c528754bd9eb4d320a7b855a3f2eb7fd73a921c74","source_file_id":"urn:uuid:271e812b-1ccd-53ed-a402-07fe58709c8a","source_locale":"en-US","source_locator":{"end_line":210,"layout":"Standard","layout_ordinal":5,"start_line":185},"source_text":"The phrase “tea time” is meant to do more than give the book a catchy title. It is meant to describe the general nature of the discourse within. Much of the material will be presented as if it were being told to a student during tea time at University, but with the benefit of careful planning. There will be no big blue boxes highlighting the main points, no stream of examples after a short introduction to a topic, and no theorem\\SpecialChar ldotsproof\\SpecialChar ldotstheorem\\SpecialChar ldotsproof structure. Instead, the necessary terms and definitions and theorems and examples will be woven into a more conversational style. My hope is that this blend of formal and informal mathematics will be easier to digest, and dare I say, students will be more invited to do their reading in this format.","source_text_sha256":"9b289b57df93e153d438d660341f6131507cdd529b69ebbaa297cbe235fffc23","translation_state":"source_frozen","unit_id":"urn:uuid:a89488a5-e6d2-538c-84eb-b3b0d487a49f"}
{"edition_id":"urn:uuid:35b4350d-7202-5d47-8b85-5262d7ca441c","id":"urn:uuid:5bec1dcc-51fe-50cb-a48b-8c09eee7481f","order":2,"protected_tokens":[{"header":"ERT","kind":"ERT","ordinal":1,"payload":"addcontentsline{toc}{chapter}{Preface} addcontentsline{toc}{section}{About Tea Time Numerical Analysis} fancyhead[RE]{Preface} fancyhead[LO]{}","sha256":"22898c92e93391789fbdadb04738024dcd49b1becf13ecc34ccbbb2acb865298"}],"record_type":"segment","rights_id":"urn:uuid:52a7c815-5b13-5f21-a52a-e7fa11238e07","schema_id":"ttna-segment-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","semantic_slot":"paragraph","source_block_sha256":"ea36d10c63990d8a8b16c143797d2f77637241506ca3479be8d155eb07f9b649","source_file_id":"urn:uuid:271e812b-1ccd-53ed-a402-07fe58709c8a","source_locale":"en-US","source_locator":{"end_line":145,"layout":"Standard","layout_ordinal":3,"start_line":110},"source_text":"{{ERT:1}}","source_text_sha256":"2a8b9e0aafed0fa1a74b1bc61c241b7812f7a0e26f97080777d7de6ca356b77e","translation_state":"source_frozen","unit_id":"urn:uuid:a89488a5-e6d2-538c-84eb-b3b0d487a49f"}
{"edition_id":"urn:uuid:35b4350d-7202-5d47-8b85-5262d7ca441c","id":"urn:uuid:5e0d1e63-8ce6-59bf-8143-be9004978394","order":8,"protected_tokens":[],"record_type":"segment","rights_id":"urn:uuid:52a7c815-5b13-5f21-a52a-e7fa11238e07","schema_id":"ttna-segment-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","semantic_slot":"paragraph","source_block_sha256":"ed0d24f122e563d2fee86b3956ac008b11ad1c83598fb0e9e41ec69444be1c7a","source_file_id":"urn:uuid:271e812b-1ccd-53ed-a402-07fe58709c8a","source_locale":"en-US","source_locator":{"end_line":359,"layout":"Standard","layout_ordinal":9,"start_line":351},"source_text":"I hope you enjoy your reading of Tea Time Numerical Analysis. It was my pleasure to write it. Feedback is always welcome.","source_text_sha256":"d22c77a0ea88b289028b343c97bbb342cdcaa58288a34fe07c66d1e294eb8a44","translation_state":"source_frozen","unit_id":"urn:uuid:a89488a5-e6d2-538c-84eb-b3b0d487a49f"}
{"edition_id":"urn:uuid:35b4350d-7202-5d47-8b85-5262d7ca441c","id":"urn:uuid:5eb1e508-6f22-522e-8afd-ef5dce88600a","order":3,"protected_tokens":[{"header":"Separator latexpar","kind":"Separator","ordinal":1,"sha256":"15d5b7744f6166dc050abaabfcffb3b41245bb1a9c6bb6d5e8e4abb21f054c38"}],"record_type":"segment","rights_id":"urn:uuid:52a7c815-5b13-5f21-a52a-e7fa11238e07","schema_id":"ttna-segment-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","semantic_slot":"paragraph","source_block_sha256":"1ff1423d5e0b2eaa9a94a5f43694628aefe7140f158b8ea6aea5248363a37095","source_file_id":"urn:uuid:271e812b-1ccd-53ed-a402-07fe58709c8a","source_locale":"en-US","source_locator":{"end_line":629,"layout":"Standard","layout_ordinal":32,"start_line":622},"source_text":"All the code appearing in the textbook can be downloaded from this textbook's companion website,","source_text_sha256":"ba76445bf443c5fd59dfa92e718224e159d608324b25f0545d0b44f85e64bf64","translation_state":"source_frozen","unit_id":"urn:uuid:767c561e-6aee-54a3-bf8c-fc3f518e3575"}
{"edition_id":"urn:uuid:35b4350d-7202-5d47-8b85-5262d7ca441c","id":"urn:uuid:67526dfb-cfe3-573f-b48e-040b33d1de02","order":5,"protected_tokens":[],"record_type":"segment","rights_id":"urn:uuid:52a7c815-5b13-5f21-a52a-e7fa11238e07","schema_id":"ttna-segment-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","semantic_slot":"paragraph","source_block_sha256":"1bf40597fa1b0d563747f7d5a9c8cc25cb70bc8ca65c8435b70e8073b07c2e71","source_file_id":"urn:uuid:271e812b-1ccd-53ed-a402-07fe58709c8a","source_locale":"en-US","source_locator":{"end_line":651,"layout":"Standard","layout_ordinal":34,"start_line":646},"source_text":"The code printed within and accompanying Tea Time Numerical Analysis electronically is distributed under the GNU Public License (GPL). Details are available at the website.","source_text_sha256":"4765ec798d03a41adae8050d9febd09f3ac8493faed2e13f96b21fc4c5ddad7b","translation_state":"source_frozen","unit_id":"urn:uuid:767c561e-6aee-54a3-bf8c-fc3f518e3575"}
{"edition_id":"urn:uuid:35b4350d-7202-5d47-8b85-5262d7ca441c","id":"urn:uuid:711a13e6-4792-5d49-94f4-7ebd49b3ae6b","order":6,"protected_tokens":[],"record_type":"segment","rights_id":"urn:uuid:52a7c815-5b13-5f21-a52a-e7fa11238e07","schema_id":"ttna-segment-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","semantic_slot":"paragraph","source_block_sha256":"f6dc35f9d5653040934e74737d98d23f65f9df28acab45496f481c53fff2db72","source_file_id":"urn:uuid:271e812b-1ccd-53ed-a402-07fe58709c8a","source_locale":"en-US","source_locator":{"end_line":503,"layout":"Standard","layout_ordinal":20,"start_line":491},"source_text":"Cocalc (Collaborative Calculation in the cloud) provides access to Octave, R, SageMath, \\SpecialChar LaTeX, C++, Julia, and a host of other kernels. Cocalc presents a much more robust environment, including classroom management features such as classes, posting and collecting assignments, collaborative editing, altogether a minimal set of tools for administering a course. They offer both free and paid account access. While they warn that running a free account may be slow, it also may suit your needs. It has been my experience that the free account requires substantial patience as connection issues and slow downs inevitably occur.","source_text_sha256":"8cfa223f44f287c2ad048f92c7f7997c7dcaf6e42f20ab90f5e6aa9794277fcf","translation_state":"source_frozen","unit_id":"urn:uuid:309948d3-a03e-5749-a53b-6f5dcf605717"}
{"edition_id":"urn:uuid:35b4350d-7202-5d47-8b85-5262d7ca441c","id":"urn:uuid:740f7926-f193-5f72-bc72-5df5178e3a2a","order":1,"protected_tokens":[],"record_type":"segment","rights_id":"urn:uuid:52a7c815-5b13-5f21-a52a-e7fa11238e07","schema_id":"ttna-segment-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","semantic_slot":"title","source_block_sha256":"d60f23d5bd28ecbe8f7c3aa46bb7795e719c9556422d40a5586e45adde6f84f5","source_file_id":"urn:uuid:271e812b-1ccd-53ed-a402-07fe58709c8a","source_locale":"en-US","source_locator":{"end_line":604,"layout":"Section*","layout_ordinal":30,"start_line":602},"source_text":"How to Get the Code","source_text_sha256":"0bc7c88d66e76a2905467500bb262d24775bf6818bdc47fb28e101e7c229189f","translation_state":"source_frozen","unit_id":"urn:uuid:767c561e-6aee-54a3-bf8c-fc3f518e3575"}
{"edition_id":"urn:uuid:35b4350d-7202-5d47-8b85-5262d7ca441c","id":"urn:uuid:7b44aebf-c709-541d-9ed9-263425fc55e7","order":1,"protected_tokens":[],"record_type":"segment","rights_id":"urn:uuid:52a7c815-5b13-5f21-a52a-e7fa11238e07","schema_id":"ttna-segment-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","semantic_slot":"title","source_block_sha256":"a4eddc4a61ca2e24e8aa0c4e0f42349347d7f8f794c4ddb696e4c1d16c15dc7f","source_file_id":"urn:uuid:271e812b-1ccd-53ed-a402-07fe58709c8a","source_locale":"en-US","source_locator":{"end_line":417,"layout":"Section*","layout_ordinal":12,"start_line":415},"source_text":"How to Get GNU Octave","source_text_sha256":"ffc481c7405163dc7cbd18cb41b2164a66af88fab425701b401dfafe4c4e254f","translation_state":"source_frozen","unit_id":"urn:uuid:bbe5e441-2af6-532c-9a0f-f3c12b3e9e40"}
{"edition_id":"urn:uuid:35b4350d-7202-5d47-8b85-5262d7ca441c","id":"urn:uuid:7b839644-f99b-5d56-96eb-04c4e461dfee","order":5,"protected_tokens":[],"record_type":"segment","rights_id":"urn:uuid:52a7c815-5b13-5f21-a52a-e7fa11238e07","schema_id":"ttna-segment-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","semantic_slot":"paragraph","source_block_sha256":"f0dbc688ef8b6629cd4a3d463bd46fa2984d8e24c67f7f546541d55470ed1f1f","source_file_id":"urn:uuid:271e812b-1ccd-53ed-a402-07fe58709c8a","source_locale":"en-US","source_locator":{"end_line":489,"layout":"Standard","layout_ordinal":19,"start_line":481},"source_text":"Octave Online is designed as an Octave interface only and includes useful features for classroom use. Open a support ticket to inquire about setting up a course. The resulting course code gives instructors the ability to see student work spaces and collaborate in real time upon their enrollment in the course. Buckets allow an instructor to post read-only code for students to import into their accounts, making it easy to distribute code for labs or assignments.","source_text_sha256":"b1cb90663854ae73ba55caca1441a67e3ff1c942dde98315865e19a2b139f622","translation_state":"source_frozen","unit_id":"urn:uuid:309948d3-a03e-5749-a53b-6f5dcf605717"}
{"edition_id":"urn:uuid:35b4350d-7202-5d47-8b85-5262d7ca441c","id":"urn:uuid:85c4926f-3405-5a4c-ab17-0e45cf2c06b8","order":7,"protected_tokens":[{"header":"Quotes eld","kind":"Quotes","ordinal":1,"sha256":"0c543e8f69a254076b2000cb6d4163dc1bfee14405a93b4a2c525aafb3ce2301"},{"header":"Quotes erd","kind":"Quotes","ordinal":2,"sha256":"f2256e820d421d857519a647df2247b25fd7f42c4ff3e95cb335b9287e332f84"}],"record_type":"segment","rights_id":"urn:uuid:52a7c815-5b13-5f21-a52a-e7fa11238e07","schema_id":"ttna-segment-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","semantic_slot":"paragraph","source_block_sha256":"4626fe1a2b48e5ce2a8efb874867f50e04a63a7aa5c28a20827e154ecdcbe598","source_file_id":"urn:uuid:271e812b-1ccd-53ed-a402-07fe58709c8a","source_locale":"en-US","source_locator":{"end_line":349,"layout":"Standard","layout_ordinal":8,"start_line":308},"source_text":"Implementation of the numerical methods in the form of computer code will also be discussed. While one could simply ignore the programming sections and exercises and still get something out of this text, it is my firm belief that full appreciation for the content can not be achieved without getting one's hands “dirty” by doing some programming. It would be nice if readers have had at least some minimal exposure to programming whether it be Python, Java, C, web programming, or just about anything, but I have made every effort to give enough detail so that even those who have never written a single line of code will be able to participate in this part of the study. In keeping with the desire to produce a completely free learning experience, GNU Octave was chosen as the programming language for this book. GNU Octave (Octave for short) is offered freely to anyone and everyone! It is free to download and use. Its source code is free to download and study. And anyone is welcome to modify or add to the code if so inclined. As an added bonus, users of the much better-known MATLAB will not be burdened by learning a new language. Octave is a MATLAB clone. By design, nearly any program written in MATLAB will run in Octave without modification. So, if you have access to MATLAB and would prefer to use it, you may do so without worry. I have made considerable effort to ensure that every line of Octave in this book will run verbatim under MATLAB. Even with this earnest effort, though, it is possible that some of the code will not run under MATLAB. It has only been tested in Octave! If you find any code that does not run in MATLAB, please let me know. Version 2.5 includes substantial rewriting of details related to Octave from installation to coding, and even includes information about computing in the cloud.","source_text_sha256":"6be85ea9f5b9ae547ef4ed0355d0a24ed340d71c4a4c03ccf825068f1125130d","translation_state":"source_frozen","unit_id":"urn:uuid:a89488a5-e6d2-538c-84eb-b3b0d487a49f"}
{"edition_id":"urn:uuid:35b4350d-7202-5d47-8b85-5262d7ca441c","id":"urn:uuid:87b25944-fb2b-5cd9-aa02-6d90dd9bfcf3","order":2,"protected_tokens":[{"command_kind":"href","header":"CommandInset href","kind":"CommandInset","ordinal":1,"sha256":"5d02bcb7d9fb143feb24896041cd4fb3314c672680c71fed439ab70fc99e80c2","target":"https://www.gnu.org/software/octave/download#ms-windows"}],"record_type":"segment","rights_id":"urn:uuid:52a7c815-5b13-5f21-a52a-e7fa11238e07","schema_id":"ttna-segment-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","semantic_slot":"paragraph","source_block_sha256":"d4b1e4996dbad4bccced9247b2752e9e9d5e29dc4d409ad0c4c84d4ec635cbf3","source_file_id":"urn:uuid:271e812b-1ccd-53ed-a402-07fe58709c8a","source_locale":"en-US","source_locator":{"end_line":519,"layout":"Standard","layout_ordinal":22,"start_line":509},"source_text":"For Windows, get an Octave installer at {{HREF:1}}.","source_text_sha256":"fabfe321c1e91307ae403c264a4e34979efbe85fbdb97487857240b5434106db","translation_state":"source_frozen","unit_id":"urn:uuid:844e0e01-ed7b-5fae-a80a-1a53eb0650e1"}
{"edition_id":"urn:uuid:35b4350d-7202-5d47-8b85-5262d7ca441c","id":"urn:uuid:8b40326d-2222-51f3-a5a8-45632b3a1743","order":6,"protected_tokens":[{"header":"Quotes eld","kind":"Quotes","ordinal":1,"sha256":"0c543e8f69a254076b2000cb6d4163dc1bfee14405a93b4a2c525aafb3ce2301"},{"header":"Quotes erd","kind":"Quotes","ordinal":2,"sha256":"f2256e820d421d857519a647df2247b25fd7f42c4ff3e95cb335b9287e332f84"}],"record_type":"segment","rights_id":"urn:uuid:52a7c815-5b13-5f21-a52a-e7fa11238e07","schema_id":"ttna-segment-v1","schema_version":"1.0.0","semantic_slot":"paragraph","source_block_sha256":"8f225cd37f28135a3cfaa79e37f43a2790d941da4dd2e441cd8387b0dd54f8ae","source_file_id":"urn:uuid:271e812b-1ccd-53ed-a402-07fe58709c8a","source_locale":"en-US","source_locator":{"end_line":306,"layout":"Standard","layout_ordinal":7,"start_line":260},"source_text":"The topical coverage in Tea Time Numerical Analysis is fairly typical. The book starts with an introductory chapter, followed by root finding methods, interpolation (part 1), numerical calculus, interpolation (part 2), and the second edition introduces a chapter on differential equations. The first five chapters cover what, at SCSU, constitutes a first semester course in numerical analysis. As this book is intended for use as a free download or an inexpensive print-on-demand volume, no effort has been made to keep the page count low or to spare copious diagrams and colors. In fact, I have taken the inexpensive mode of delivery as liberty to do quite the opposite. I have added many passages and diagrams that are not strictly necessary for the study of numerical analysis, but are at least peripherally related, and may be of interest to some readers. Most of these passages will be presented as digressions, so they will be easy to identify. For example, Taylor's theorem plays such a central role in the subject that not only its statement is presented. Its proof and a bit of history are added as “crumpets”. Of course they can be skipped, but are included to provide a more complete understanding of this fundamental theorem of numerical analysis. For another example, as a fan of dynamical systems, I found it impossible to refrain from including a section on visualizing Newton's Method. The powerful and beautiful pictures of Newton's Method as a dynamical system should be eyebrow-raising and question-provoking even if only tangentially important. There are, of course, other examples of somewhat less critical content, but each is there to enhance the reader's understanding or appreciation of the subject, even if the material is not strictly necessary for an introductory study of numerical analysis. While version 2.5 does not introduce any new sections, it contains many corrections, new exercises and modified discourse. As a result, page and exercise numbering has changed.","source_text_sha256":"7a71cf51f872c8cb90528409a89b9b560d878573daace061641925574021ac74","translation_state":"source_frozen","unit_id":"urn:uuid:a89488a5-e6d2-538c-84eb-b3b0d487a49f"}
